# Runners this machine can create. Copy this file to runner.conf and fill in
# your own repos. That copy is gitignored, since it names your own GitHub
# repositories, which is a property of the machine that hosts the runner,
# not of this project.
#
# abgal github-runner create reads the line whose name matches -n. Every
# column can also be overridden on the command line, for a runner not
# listed here at all.
#
# Columns, separated by |:
#
#   name      the runner's name, also its systemd service and the name
#             config.sh registers it under
#   repo      owner/repo it registers against
#   labels    comma separated, passed to config.sh --labels
#   backend   host or container
#
# name    | repo                  | labels          | backend
ci-01     | myorg/myrepo          | linux,x64       | host
